    "title": "Pregnant woman: VL due at 3 months on ART",
    "message": "Guidelines state that HIV-positive pregnant women newly initiated on ART at ANC should have a viral load test at 3 months on ART. Patient initiated ART 10 weeks ago (approximately 2.5 months), so the 3-month VL is not yet due but is imminent. The current VL of 89 copies/mL was presumably obtained early; guidelines specify the 3-month timepoint. No clinician plan was documented today, so it is unclear whether the 3-month VL has been scheduled. Ensuring timely VL monitoring is critical for this pregnant patient to confirm suppression and guide decisions about preventing vertical transmission.",
