    "title": "Cotrimoxazole preventive therapy missing",
    "message": "Guidelines prioritize cotrimoxazole preventive therapy (CPT) for all PLHIV newly initiating ART and for pregnant and breastfeeding women. Patient is both newly initiated on ART (10 weeks ago) and pregnant at 22 weeks, meeting two prioritized categories. CPT reduces risk of malaria, diarrhoea, pneumonia, hospitalization, and mortality. Patient is not currently on CPT and no plan to initiate it was documented. Note that additional intermittent preventive treatment for malaria using sulfadoxine-pyrimethamine is not required for pregnant women already on CPT.",
