    "title": "Mild anaemia with TDF renal trend",
    "message": "Guidelines list severe anaemia as a toxicity of AZT (Hb <8 mg/dL triggers substitution with TDF) and note that TDF can cause Fanconi syndrome. Patient's Hb is 10.8 g/dL, which is mildly low for pregnancy (physiological anaemia of pregnancy is common). TDF is not a direct cause of anaemia, but if TDF needs to be substituted due to declining renal function, AZT would be contraindicated as the alternative if anaemia worsens. Current Hb does not meet the <8 g/dL threshold for action. Iron supplementation with ferrous sulfate is already prescribed, which is appropriate management for pregnancy-related anaemia.",
